// How this repository is deployed, in this repository.
// ADR-0097 is why this file exists rather than a set of dashboard fields, and why wrangler is a dev
// dependency of a repository that allowed four.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// It is here because there is nowhere else to put it
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The first build failed with the Cloudflare application detection logic having "been run in the root
// of a workspace instead of targeting a specific project", which is what a monorepo with no
// configuration file looks like from outside. `pages_build_output_dir` below is what answers it.
//
// So the two halves of a deployment live in two places and only one of them can drift. The build
// command and the deploy command are fields of a dashboard - `pnpm run site:build` and
// `wrangler pages deploy`, both of them constants carrying no version and no path - and everything
// that is a decision is here.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What is deliberately not here
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// **No custom domain, although one is connected.** `https://toopo.dev` serves this tree as of
// `994374d` and it is attached in the dashboard, not here - because a custom domain is a fact about
// which names point at a project and wrangler's Pages configuration has no field for it. That is a
// gap in this file's own claim to hold every decision, and it is written down rather than left to be
// discovered: what was decided here is what is deployed, and where it answers from is decided next
// door. ADR-0103 carries the measurement of what that address serves.
//
// **No `main`.** Nothing here runs code: a Pages project serving a folder needs no script, and
// permanent rule 1 refuses runtime indirection in any case. What decides how a response is served is
// `_headers`, which `packages/site/served-headers.ts` derives from the endpoints and the build writes
// into the tree.
//
// **No `html_handling`.** Its default, `auto-trailing-slash`, serves `<contract>/index.html` at
// `<contract>/` - which is the address `linkTo` publishes, the address the sitemap carries, and the
// address a contract's licence header cites. Declaring the default would be a second statement of
// something already true.
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "toopo",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-16",

  // Written by `pnpm run site:build`, which runs from the workspace root and is not committed: a
  // rendering of the catalogue is not a contract, an implementation, a test or the evidence a run
  // produced, and `.gitignore` keeps it out.
  //
  // `pages_build_output_dir` and not `assets.directory`, and that one field is the whole migration.
  // ADR-0100 carries the measurement: the two mechanisms were deployed one variable apart, and this one
  // answers the published address with 200 and serves the `Cache-Control` `_headers` declares at the
  // address that serves the bytes. The other answered a redirect and applied the rule to the redirect.
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./packages/site/out"
}
